Babel
=====

This Play 2.3.10 / Scala 2.11.12 application builds with Maven and JDK 8.
Set JAVA_HOME to a JDK 8 installation; the legacy compiler does not support
newer JDKs.

Build on macOS/Linux:
  ./mvnw -DskipTests clean verify

Build on Windows:
  mvnw.cmd -DskipTests clean verify

The wrapper downloads Maven 3.9.16 and dependencies on first use. No system
Maven installation is required. Bundled libraries in lib/ are used directly.
Maven compiles the app/ sources, Play routes and templates, and test/ sources,
and packages conf/, config/, resources/, and public/ assets.

Run the application from the repository root:
  ./mvnw play2:run

BabelNet data and WordNet must be installed separately. Set babelnet.dir and
jlt.wordnetPrefix in config/jlt.var.properties and the corresponding override
in config/babelnet.var.properties for your installation;
review the other config/*.var.properties paths as well. Keep the config/ and
resources/ directories available when running from the repository root.

Run all tests after configuring these external datasets:
  ./mvnw clean verify

The existing request and browser tests initialize BabelNet. CI builds and
compiles the tests with -DskipTests because the external datasets are not
included in this repository. The legacy browser test also currently fails
with a JVM VerifyError (Cannot inherit from final class).
